    6   
    7                 /       MUST BE ASSEMBLED WITH '/J' [OS/8 PAL8 '/F'] OPTION SWITCH SET.
    8   
    9                 /       P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER FOR PRIMARY TD8E [DEVICE CODE 77] WITH TU56H [ONE
   10                 /       DRIVE ONLY] OR TU56 [TWO DRIVES].
   11   
   12                 /       AUTOMATICALLY REMEMBERS PROPER INITIAL SEARCH DIRECTION WHEN THE LOGICAL
   13                 /       CONSOLE OVERLAY IS IN EFFECT; OTHERWISE ALWAYS STARTS SEARCHES IN REVERSE
   14                 /       SIMILAR TO TC12.  [NOTE: THIS APPLIES TO CALLS FOR EITHER LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT.]
   15   
   16                 /       IGNORES THE TWO HIGH-ORDER BITS OF THE LOGICAL UNIT FOR ALL CALLS.  THUS, THE
   17                 /       CALL CANNOT DISTINGUISH BETWEEN DRIVES 0, 2, 4, 6 OR 1, 3, 5, 7; FUTURE
   18                 /       RELEASES WILL CAUSE A SELECT ERROR ON LOGICAL UNITS 2 THROUGH 7 WHEN THE
   19                 /       LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS IN EFFECT.  [NOTE: THE MR8E-C ROM ONLY SUPPORTS THE
   20                 /       DEVICE 77 TD8E CONTROLLER; NON-SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLERS CAPABLE OF SUPPORTING 4
   21                 /       TD8E CONTROLLERS AND UP TO EIGHT DRIVES WILL EVENTUALLY BE IMPLEMENTED.]
   22   
   23                 /       CAN ONLY BE BOOTSTRAPPED TO LOGICAL DRIVE UNIT 0.  THIS IS A RESTRICTION OF
   24                 /       THE MR8E-C ROM.  ALTERNATE BOOTSTRAPS MAY BE DEVELOPED IN FUTURE RELEASES TO
   25                 /       OVERCOME THIS [WITH DIFFICULTY].
   26   
   27                 /       THE BASIC DEVICE HANDLER HALTS/RETRIES ON ALL ERRORS DETECTED BY THE ROM.  DUE
   28                 /       TO LACK OF SPACE IN FIELD 0, THE ROM-BASED RETRY COUNT LOGIC IS NOT SUPPORTED.
   29                 /       HOWEVER, IN KEEPING WITH THE P?S/8 PHILOSOPHY OF NOT OBFUSCATING HARDWARE
   30                 /       PROBLEMS, THIS DESIGN DECISION WOULD APPLY EVEN IF THE CODE SPACE WERE
   31                 /       AVAILABLE.  IT IS NECESSARY TO MAKE THE USER AWARE OF DEGRADING HARDWARE
   32                 /       SITUATIONS; THIS CAN ONLY BE REALIZED BY ALERTING THE USER WITH APPROPRIATE
   33                 /       ERROR HANDLING.  WHEN THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS IN EFFECT, THE NATURE OF
   34                 /       THE ERROR WILL BE EVEN MORE OBVIOUS.  HOWEVER, PROPERLY FUNCTIONING EQUIPMENT
   35                 /       AND DECTAPE MEDIA DOES NOT ROUTINELY CAUSE ERRORS; THEY SHOULD BE TREATED AS A
   36                 /       SIGN OF IMPENDING FAILURE OF THE DRIVE GUIDES AND/OR THE DECTAPE MEDIA.  IF
   37                 /       TAKEN CARE OF EARLY, ALL DATA ON THE DECTAPE SHOULE BE RECOVERABLE BEFORE THE
   38                 /       PROBLEM WORSENS.  [NOTE: THE RETRY COUNT IS USED THROUGHOUT OS/8 DECTAPE
   39                 /       HANDLING AND IS THE ROOT CAUSE OF THIS PROBLEM; BY PROPER DESIGN, THIS
   40                 /       "FEATURE" WITHIN THE MR8E-C IS AVOIDED.]
   41   
   42                 /       INTERRUPT STATUS IS RESTORED AFTER A CALL TO THE SYSTEM HANDLER; INTERNALLY,
   43                 /       THE HANDLER OPERATES WITH INTERRUPTS OFF TO PREVENT TIMING PROBLEMS.  WHILE
   44                 /       THERE IS NO RULES REGARDING THIS THROUGHOUT P?S/8, GIVEN THAT THE TD8E IS TO
   45                 /       BE USED ONLY ON OMNIBUS MACHINES ALLOWS THIS FEATURE TO BE ADDED.  [NOTE: DUE
   46                 /       TO SPEED CONSIDERATIONS, IT IS RECOMMENDED THE TD8E ONLY BE USED WHERE THE
   47                 /       KK8E CPU IS AVAILABLE [PDP-8/E, PDP-8/F, PDP-8/M AND PDP-8/A-600 SERIES].
   48                 /       THIS IS ESPECIALLY PROBLEMATIC WHEN THE MR8E-C IS IN USE DUE TO THE OVERHEAD
   49                 /       CAUSED BY INTER-FIELD SUBROUTINE CALLS.
   50   
   51                 /       ADDITIONAL NOTEWORTHY FEATURES WILL BE DESCRIBED HERE AS THE BINARY IMAGE CODE
   52                 /       IS DISSASSEMBLED.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 2

   54                 /       NOTE: CERTAIN FEATURES OF THE HANDLER ARE BASED ON THE RECOLLECTION OF
   55                 /       CHARLES LASNER, P?S NY, WHO HASTILY WROTE THE ORIGINAL VERSION 40 YEARS AGO,
   56                 /       WHEN BRIEFLY AN APPROPRIATE PDP-8/E WITH TD8E AND MR8E-C CONFIGURATION WAS
   57                 /       AVAILABLE DURING A TRANSIENT PROGRAMMING ASSIGNMENT.  DUE TO CIRCUMSTANCES,
   58                 /       THIS SYSTEM CONFIGURATION WAS NEVER UPDATED; THE ORIGINAL SOURCE CODE IS NOT
   59                 /       AVAILABLE AND PRESUMED PERMANENTLY LOST.  IT IS KNOWN THAT THE SOURCE CODE OF
   60                 /       THE MR8E-C ROM WAS INCLUDED WITHIN THE SOURCE FILE OF THE HANDLER TO ALLOW
   61                 /       OCCASIONAL DEVELOPMENT CONSISTENT WITH THE OVERALL EVOLVEMENT OF P?S/8.
   62                 /       HOWEVER, NO SIGNIFICANT CHANGES TO P?S/8 OF ANY RELEVANCE TO THE TD8E WERE
   63                 /       MADE AFTER THE LAST KNOWN CONTACT WITH AN ALTERNATE PDP-8/E SYSTEM IN 1976
   64                 /       [AND PERHAPS THE EARLY PART OF 1977.  THE LAST KNOWN SYSTEM CONSISTED OF A
   65                 /       TU56H, TD8E AND 32K OF CORE MEMORY [AND UNRELATED PERIPHERALS].  THE MR8E-C
   66                 /       ROM IMAGE WAS LOADED BEFORE BOOTING THE SYSTEM TO ALLOW CREATING AN IMAGE OF A
   67                 /       FUNCTIONAL SYSTEM FOR TESTING.
   68   
   69                 /       DUE TO THE CIRCUMSTANCES OF P?S/8 DEVELOPMENT, ALL TD8E-SPECIFIC CODE WAS
   70                 /       STRIPPED OUT OF THE TYPICAL SET OF DEVELOPMENTAL SOURCE FILES DUE TO FILE SIZE
   71                 /       LIMITATIONS.  DUE TO THE APPLICABLE LOGISTICS, ALL DEVELOPMENT FILES WERE
   72                 /       SPLIT INTO TWO SECTIONS EACH CAPABLE OF BEING STORED ON HALF OF AN RK8E/RK05
   73                 /       PACK.  IT WAS IMPRACTICAL TO PHYSICALLY TRANSPORT THE MEDIA; DECISIONS WERE
   74                 /       MADE TO SPLIT OFF THE TD8E-RELATED FILES [AS WELL AS CERTAIN OTHER FILES
   75                 /       RELEVANT TO OTHER CONFIGURATIONS].  IT IS HOPED THE SOURCE FILES FOR THESE
   76                 /       OTHER CONFIGURATIONS CAN BE RECONSTRUCTED FROM SURVIVING BINARY MEDIA; IF THIS
   77                 /       CANNOT BE ACCOMPLISHED, THE CONFIGURATION WILL REQUIRE COMPLETE SOURCE
   78                 /       RECREATION AND ACCESS TO THE APPLICABLE HARDWARE AT THE MINIMUM.  NOTE:
   79                 /       CERTAIN ENHANCEMENTS TO THE SOURCE CODE SPECIFIC TO THESE SYSTEMS WILL ALSO
   80                 /       REQUIRE ADDITIONAL CONTACT WITH THE RELEVANT HARDWARE; P?S/8 DEVELOPMENT
   81                 /       IS NOW ACTIVE AGAIN AFTER A SHORT RECESS OF ABOUT 22 YEARS.  SOME OF THESE
   82                 /       ISSUES WILL BE RESOLVED AS TIME PERMITS AS WELL AS ACCESS TO THE RELEVANT
   83                 /       HARDWARE.  THE TD8E ISSUES WILL BE RESOLVED USING THE SIMH PDP-8 SIMULATOR
   84                 /       FOLLOWED BY PERIODIC TESTING ON TD8E-BASED PDP-8/E HARDWARE.
   85   
   86                 /       UNTIL ALL TD8E-SPECIFIC CODE CAN BE DISASSEMBLED FROM THE RECENTLY RECOVERED
   87                 /       VERSION 8T DECTAPE, IT IS NOT CLEAR IF THIS TAPE REPRESENTS THE FINAL POINT IN
   88                 /       THE DEVELOPMENT OF THIS SYSTEM.  CERTAIN COMPONENTS NOT YET CONFIRMED SHOULD
   89                 /       PROVIDE PLAUSIBLE ANSWERS.  [IT IS KNOWN THERE WAS A SPECIAL INTERACTION
   90                 /       BETWEEN THIS HARDWARE CONFIGURATION AND THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY WHEN
   91                 /       CONFIGURED EXPRESSLY FOR THE VT8E.]


