   93                 /       PROGRAM EDIT HISTORY.
   94   
   95                 /       01-APR-1975     -       ORIGINAL RELEASE OF THE BINARY CODE [ESTIMATED]; THIS
   96                 /                               IS LIKELY THE ONLY SURVIVING COPY OF THE P?S/8
   97                 /                               OPERATING SYSTEM FOR THE TD8E/MR8E-C.  MOST OF THE
   98                 /                               SOURCE CODE WILL BE OBTAINED BY DISASSEMBLY OF THIS
   99                 /                               RELEASE RECOVERED ON A SURVIVING DECTAPE.
  100   
  101                 /                               NOTE: IT IS SUSPECTED THIS IS THE ONLY KNOWN SURVIVING
  102                 /                               COPY OF THE CONFIGURATION FOR THE TD8E WITH MR8E-C
  103                 /                               ROM.  IT IS LIKELY IT WAS NOT PROPERLY TESTED.  AS OF
  104                 /                               THIS WRITING, IT IS NOW KNOWN THE CONFIGURATION IS
  105                 /                               FATALLY FLAWED, BUT TENTATIVELY FUNCTIONAL BY A
  106                 /                               CONTRIVED KLUDGE THAT WAS APPARENTLY APPLIED AFTER
  107                 /                               USING ANY P?S/8 OPERATION THAT MODIFIED BLOCK 0000.
  108                 /                               LATER RELEASES WILL OVERCOME THIS BY MAKING FURTHER
  109                 /                               CHANGES IN THE DESIGN WHICH WILL CORRECT THE PROBLEM.
  110                 /                               THE ONLY KNOWN PROBLEM THAT CANNOT BE OVERCOME IS THAT
  111                 /                               THE DESIGN CHANGE WILL ELIMINATE THE FATAL PROBLEM,
  112                 /                               BUT THE SYSTEM BOOTUP PROCEDURE WILL REQUIRE AN
  113                 /                               ADDITIONAL TAPE TURN-AROUND.  [USERS OF THE TC01/TC08
  114                 /                               RELEASE OF P?S/8 MAY NOTICE THIS TINY LOSS OF
  115                 /                               PERFORMANCE; BY CONTRAST, OS/8 BOOTUP TAKES MUCH MORE
  116                 /                               TIME THAN EITHER RELEASE.]
  117   
  118                 /       18-DEC-2015     -       IMAGE OF THE 1975 RELEASE AVAILABLE FOR USE WITH THE
  119                 /                               SIMH PDP-8 SIMULATOR.  EXAMINATION OF THE TAPE
  120                 /                               CONFIRMS IT IS A SYSTEM CREATED SOMETIME IN 1974/1975.
  121                 /                               HOWEVER, THE TAPE CANNOT BE BOOTED BECAUSE THE IMAGE
  122                 /                               OF THE MR8E-C ROM IS NOT AVAILABLE TO THE SIMH PDP-8
  123                 /                               SIMULATOR.
  124   
  125                 /       26-JAN-2016     -       OPERATIONAL PRE-FINAL RELEASE OF THE SOURCE CODE OF
  126                 /                               THE MR8E-C ROM IS COMPLETED.  USING THE MR8E-C BINARY
  127                 /                               IMAGE, THE ORIGINAL RELEASE IS BOOTED ON THE SIMH
  128                 /                               PDP-8 SIMULATOR; ALTHOUGH THIS IS A VERY OLD RELEASE
  129                 /                               OF P?S/8 [APPARENTLY VERSION 8T BASED ON ASSOCIATED
  130                 /                               DECTAPE PACKAGING], MOST OF THE BASIC ELEMENTS OF
  131                 /                               DEVICE-SPECIFIC FUNCTIONALITY ARE CONFIRMED WORKING ON
  132                 /                               THE SIMH PDP-8 SIMULATOR [OTHER THAN OPERATIONS THAT
  133                 /                               MODIFY THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0000 SUCH AS THE "DATE"
  134                 /                               COMMAND, WHICH WRITES THE CURRENT DATE VALUE ON THE
  135                 /                               DECTAPE].  DISASSEMBLY WILL PROCEED FOR IDENTIFIABLE
  136                 /                               ELEMENTS; DIRECT BINARY COMPARISON WILL BE USED TO
  137                 /                               CONFIRM SOURCE FILE AUTHENTICITY.  UNTIL THIS IS
  138                 /                               ACCOMPLISHED, ANY IDEAS REGARDING CODE IMPROVEMENT
  139                 /                               WILL BE DEFERRED; HOWEVER, CERTAIN TENTATIVE CHANGES
  140                 /                               ARE BEING MADE TO THE SOURCE FILE AS COMMENTS TO BE
  141                 /                               CONSIDERED AFTER ALL RECOVERABLE SOURCE CODE
  142                 /                               OPERATIONS HAVE CONCLUDED.


