/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 5

  190                 /                               THIS IS POOR DESIGN SINCE THAT MEANS THAT SHOULD A
  191                 /                               TD8E DECTAPE BE ACCESSED ON A TC01/TC08 [OR OTHER
  192                 /                               POTENTIAL PROBLEMATIC INTERACTION] OCCUR, THE "BIN"
  193                 /                               PROGRAM ON THAT SYSTEM WILL LOAD THE INCORRECT SLURP
  194                 /                               LOADER.  WHILE THERE CANNOT BE PROTECTION FROM THIS IN
  195                 /                               GENERAL [AS CERTAIN SYSTEM CONVENTIONS ONLY CHANGE
  196                 /                               SLOWLY IF AT ALL], THIS SYSTEM IS SO FAR REMOVED FROM
  197                 /                               NEWER RELEASES, THE ABILITY TO EVEN ACCESS "BIN" FROM
  198                 /                               THESE EARLIER RELEASES IS ACTUALLY IMPOSSIBLE [AND WHY
  199                 /                               THE DECTAPE HAD TO BE SEARCHED MANUALLY TO EVEN LOCATE
  200                 /                               THE CODE!].  HOWEVER, THE NEWER DESIGN ELIMINATES
  201                 /                               DEVICE-DEPENDENT CODE FROM THE "BIN" PROGRAM AND
  202                 /                               PLACES THE COMPONENT ON AN IMPLIED SYSTEM BLOCK.
  203                 /                               THUS, IF ALL SYSTEMS ARE WITHIN A CLOSE RANGE OF
  204                 /                               RELEASE, THIS PROBLEM IS ELIMINATED AS THE SLURP
  205                 /                               LOADER WILL ALWAYS BE READ FROM THE IMPLIED BLOCK ON
  206                 /                               THE SYSTEM DEVICE LOGICAL UNIT FOR BOOTUP.
  207   
  208                 /                               NOTE: THE '/I' DEVICE HANDLER RELOAD CODE HAS ALSO
  209                 /                               BEEN LOCATED; THIS CAN BE WORKED ON ONCE THE SLURP
  210                 /                               LOADER HAS BEEN COMPLETELY DOCUMENTED AT THE SOURCE
  211                 /                               LEVEL, ETC.  [NOTE: FORTUNATELY, WHILE THESE BLOCK
  212                 /                               ASSIGNMENTS HAVE CHANGED OVER THE YEARS, THE OVERALL
  213                 /                               FUNCTIONALITY HAS NOT, ALTHOUGH A FEW MINOR
  214                 /                               ADDITIONAL LIMITATIONS MAY APPLY THAT WILL REQUIRE
  215                 /                               MODIFICATION FOR FUTURE RELEASES [AS WELL AS FOR USE
  216                 /                               WITH THE PRESENT RELEASE VERSION 8Z].  ALSO, ANY
  217                 /                               CHANGES MADE TO OVERCOME THE FATAL FLAW MAY INTERACT
  218                 /                               WITH THIS ASPECT OF THE OPERATING SYSTEM AND THUS
  219                 /                               AFFECT CERTAIN SPECIFICS OF THE RELOAD; THE RELOAD
  220                 /                               CONCEPT INTERACTS THREE SPECIFIC PORTIONS OF THE
  221                 /                               SYSTEM CONFIGURATION: 1) THE SPECIFICS OF THE SYSTEM
  222                 /                               DEVICE HANDLER WHICH WILL BE UNDERGOING NECESSARY
  223                 /                               CHANGES TO OVERCOME THE FATAL FLAW, 2) THE SLURP
  224                 /                               LOADER SPECIFICS THAT WILL BE MODIED, AND 3) THE
  225                 /                               RELOAD BLOCK ITSELF AS NECESSARY; ALL THREE MUST BE
  226                 /                               UPDATED IN A COOPERATIVE EFFORT TO ACHIEVE A WORKABLE
  227                 /                               RELEASE FOR ANY SYSTEM DEVICE THAT SUPPORTS A SLURP
  228                 /                               LOADER.]  [NOTE: ALL TAPE-BASED SYSTEMS AND RX-BASED
  229                 /                               SYSTEMS SUPPORT A SLURP LOADER AND FEW ELSE.  DEVICES
  230                 /                               THAT RUN ON VERY FAST OR ONE-CYCLE DMA INTERFACES
  231                 /                               MUST ALWAYS USE THE VIRTUAL LOADER WHICH IS ALWAYS AN
  232                 /                               OPTION FOR ALL SYSTEMS [BUT MAY BE DEFAULT ON THESE
  233                 /                               HIGHER-PERFORMANCE CONFIGURATIONS].]
  234   
  235                 /                               THE REWIND AND UNLOAD ROUTINES ARE NOW ROUGHED OUT,
  236                 /                               BUT NOT FLESHED OUT YET; THE DEVICE SIZE PATCH IS
  237                 /                               NOW PRESENT.


