  306                 /                               LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY; THE TD8E SYSTEM DEVICE
  307                 /                               SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER CAN CLEARLY BENEFIT FROM THE
  308                 /                               KIND OF ENHANCEMENT PROVIDED FOR OTHER DEVICES SUCH AS
  309                 /                               THE TC01/TC08 DECTAPE.
  310   
  311                 /                               FROM THE RECOLLECTIONS OF CHARLES LASNER, IT WOULD
  312                 /                               APPEAR SOME MEASURE OF OVERLAY SUPPORT WAS ADDED.
  313                 /                               HOWEVER, IT IS POSSIBLE THIS IS A PRELIMINARY RELEASE
  314                 /                               CREATED FOR EXPEDIENT PURPOSES;  THE CODE MAY SIMPLY
  315                 /                               NOT BE PRESENT ON THIS PARTICULAR SYSTEM IMAGE FROM
  316                 /                               THE RECOVERED DECTAPE.  MOREOVER, ESPECIALLY IN LIGHT
  317                 /                               OF THE FATAL FLAW DISCOVERED IN THE LOGIC OF THE
  318                 /                               SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER [PREVENTING MODIFICATION OF
  319                 /                               BLOCK 0000 WITHOUT SOME EXTERNAL REMEDY APPLIED AFTER
  320                 /                               THE FACT], IT IS LIKELY THAT AT LEAST SOME PORTION OF
  321                 /                               THIS SUPPORT NEVER EXISTED BEFORE.  A COMPLETED FUTURE
  322                 /                               RELEASE OF A SYSTEM FOR THE TD8E/MR8E-C ROM SHOULD
  323                 /                               INCLUDE ALL SUCH IMPROVEMENTS [AS WELL AS RESOLVING
  324                 /                               THE FATAL FLAW AND RECONCILING CERTAIN SYSTEM
  325                 /                               DEFINITIONS THAT HAVE CHANGED OVER THE YEARS].
  326                 /                               CERTAIN OF THESE CHANGES HAVE BEEN DOCUMENTED IN THE
  327                 /                               SOURCE CODE IN THE FORM OF COMMENTS; HOWEVER,
  328                 /                               ADDITIONAL WORK IS REQUIRED TO PRODUCE A COMPLETELY
  329                 /                               FUNCTIONAL SYSTEM AS INTENDED [FOR VERSION 8Z AND
  330                 /                               COMPATIBILITY WITH THE FUTURE REQUIREMENTS OF VERSION
  331                 /                               9A WHICH IS CURRENTLY IN DESIGN DEVELOPMENT].
  332   
  333                 /                               DEPENDING ON THE LEAD TIME FOR FURTHER WORK ON THIS
  334                 /                               CONFIGURATION, A PROVISIONAL SYSTEM MAY BE PRODUCED TO
  335                 /                               PROVIDE NOMINAL COMPATIBILITY WITH VERSION 8Z TO
  336                 /                               ALLOW TESTING ON BOTH THE SIMH SIMULATOR AND ALSO ON
  337                 /                               AVAILABLE HARDWARE.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 8

  339                 /                               IT IS BECOMING INCREASINGLY CLEAR THAT THIS SPECIFIC
  340                 /                               CONFIGURATION CANNOT SUPPORT BOOTUP FROM DRIVE UNIT 1.
  341                 /                               AS SUCH, REFERENCES TO THIS WILL EVENTUALLY BE REMOVED
  342                 /                               FROM ALL SOURCE CODE.  [THE NON-ROM TD8E WITH EXTENDED
  343                 /                               MEMORY SYSTEM VARIANT COULD STILL SUPPORT SUCH AN
  344                 /                               EXTENDED BOOTSTRAP; WHERE CODE IS INCLUDED FOR FUTURE
  345                 /                               USE IN DEVELOPING THAT ALTERNATIVE SYSTEM, DRIVE 1
  346                 /                               REFERENCES WILL BE RETAINED BUT NOTED THAT THE CODE
  347                 /                               IS PROVIDED [OR COMMENTED ON] PRESUMING THIS IS
  348                 /                               POSSIBLE [IF ONLY IN THEORY].


