/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 12

  495                 /       TD8E BOOTSTRAP METHODS.
  496   
  497                 /       1.      MR8E-C ROM TD8E BOOTSTRAP.
  498   
  499                 /       ASSUMING THE MR8E-C ROM IS AVAILABLE [WHICH IS A REQUIRMEMENT OF THIS SYSTEM
  500                 /       CONFIGURATION], THE FOLLOWING IS THE SHORTEST WAY TO BOOTSTRAP ANY COMPATIBLE
  501                 /       TD8E OPERATING SYSTEM [ON LOGICAL UNIT 0 ONLY] BY THE USE OF AN EXECUTABLE
  502                 /       PROGRAM.  [USING THE FRONT PANEL SWITCH REGISTER TO BOOTSTRAP THE SYSTEM IS
  503                 /       ESSENTIALLY THE MANUAL EQUIVALENT OF THIS PROGRAM.]
  504   
  505                         NOPUNCH                         /PREVENT BINARY OUTPUT; THIS SECTION IS FOR
  506                                                         /DOCUMENTATION PURPOSES ONLY.
  507   
  508          *0200          *200                            /ANYWHERE ON ANY PAGE OF ANY FIELD.
  509   
  510                 /       CLA                             /THE AC MUST BE CLEAR.
  511                 /       IOF                             /INTERRUPTS MUST BE OFF.
  512                 /       CDF     XX                      /THE DATA FIELD IS IGNORED.
  513   000200  6272          CIF     70                      /GOING TO ROM FIELD.
  514   000201* 5602          JMP I   .+1;    ROMBOOT         /START THE BOOTSTRAP WITHIN THE ROM.
  515   000202* 7470 
  516   
  517                 /       NOTE: THIS BOOTSTRAP CAN BE SHORTENED BY ONE INSTRUCTION BY LOADING ANYWHERE
  518                 /       ON PAGE 36 [7400-7577].  THE "JMP I" INSTRUCTION CAN THEN BE REPLACED BY
  519                 /       "JMP ROMBOOT"; THE ADDRESS POINTER TO "ROMBOOT" BECOMES SUPERFLUOUS.
  520   
  521                 /       2.      STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP.
  522   
  523                         NOPUNCH                         /PREVENT BINARY OUTPUT; THIS SECTION IS FOR
  524                                                         /DOCUMENTATION PURPOSES ONLY.
  525   
  526           0000          FIELD   0                       /LOADS IN FIELD 0.
  527   
  528          *7300          *7300                           /THIS IS WHERE THE STANDALONE BOOTSTRAP LOADS.
  529   
  530   007300* 1312  K1000,  TAD     GET/(2000)              /GET REVERSE DIRECTION BIT.  ALSO CONSTANT
  531                                                         /1000 [ONLY THE HIGH-ORDER FOUR BITS ARE USED].
  532   007301* 4312          JMS     GET                     /LOCATE REVERSE END ZONE.
  533   007302* 4312          JMS     GET                     /LOOK FOR 31 CODE GOING FORWARD.
  534   007303* 6773  RD,     SDSQ                            /QUAD FLAG UP?
  535   007304* 5303          JMP     .-1                     /NO, WAIT FOR IT.
  536   007305* 6777          SDRD                            /YES, READ IT IN.
  537   007306* 3726          DCA I   WCT                     /STORE IT INTO MEMORY.
  538   007307* 2326          ISZ     WCT                     /BUMP TO NEXT; ALL DONE YET?
  539   007310* 5303          JMP     RD                      /NO, KEEP GOING.
  540   
  541                 /       AT THIS POINT BLOCK 0000 HAS BEEN READ INTO 07360-07557 AND BLOCK 0001 HAS
  542                 /       BEEN READ INTO 07600-07777.  [NOTE: ONLY OS/8 AND COS-300/310 REQUIRE THE
  543                 /       BLOCK OOO1 DATA LOAD; EDU-SYSTEM 15/30 AND P?S/8  ONLY REQUIRE BLOCK 0000
  544                 /       LOADING INTO MEMORY.]  FOR ALL SUPPORTED SYSTEMS, THE OFFSET LOADING INTO
  545                 /       FIELD 0 7360-7557 WILL BE EXPECTED AND DEALT WITH ACCORDINGLY.
  546   
  547   007311* 5732          JMP I   STRT/(STARTIT)          /GO START IT UP.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 13

  549                 /       GET TO DESIRED MARK WINDOW VALUE ROUTINE.  [NOTE: INITIALIZED TO SAVE A WORD.]
  550   
  551   007312* 2000  GET,    2000                            /GET TO DESIRED MARK ROUTINE.
  552   007313* 1300          TAD     K1000/(1000)            /ADD ON UNIT [0] AND GO BITS TO DIRECTION BIT
  553                                                         /PASSED IN AC.  NOTE: LOW-ORDER BITS IGNORED.
  554   007314* 6774          SDLC                            /LOAD COMMAND REGISTER TO START THE TAPE MOVING.
  555   007315* 6771  MRKSRCH,SDSS                            /NEW LINE IN?
  556   007316* 5315          JMP     .-1                     /NO, WAIT FOR IT.
  557   007317* 6776          SDRC                            /YES, READ THE COMMAND REGISTER.
  558   007320* 0331          AND     K77/(77)                /JUST MARK WINDOW BITS.
  559   
  560                 /       THE FIRST TIME THIS ROUTINE IS USED, THE REVERSE END ZONE MARK VALUE IS
  561                 /       SEARCHED FOR; THE SECOND TIME, THE 31 CODE IS SEARCHED FOR.
  562   
  563   007321* 1327  MARKSEL,TAD     MRKVALUE                /COMPARE TO DESIRED [END MARK OR 31 CODE].
  564   007322* 7640          SZA CLA                         /SKIP IF IT MATCHES.
  565   007323* 5315          JMP     MRKSRCH                 /GO BACK IF NOT.
  566   007324* 2321          ISZ     MARKSEL                 /BUMP TO NEXT MARK CODE FOR NEXT TIME.
  567   007325* 5712          JMP I   GET                     /RETURN TO CALLER.
  568   
  569   007326* 7354  WCT,    BOOTBUFFER                      /WORD COUNT AND STORE POINTER.
  570   
  571   007327* 7756  MRKVALU,-22;    -31                     /REVERSE END AND 31 CODE MARK CONSTANTS.
  572   007330* 7747 
  573   007331* 0077  K77,    77                              /CONSTANT 0077.
  574   007332* 7400  STRT,   STARTIT                         /WHERE TO START THE BOOT CODE READ IN.
  575   
  576   007333* 0000          ZBLOCK  7354-.                  /EMPTY SPACE.
  577   
  578           7354          BOOTBUF=.                       /DECTAPE BLOCK 0000 CONTENTS START LOADING HERE.
  579   
  580   007354* 0000          ZBLOCK  4                       /THESE LOCATIONS ARE LOADED WITH PRE-DATA WORDS.
  581   
  582           7360          BLKDATA=.                       /THE DATA WORDS FROM BLOCK 0000 LOAD HERE.
  583   
  584   007360* 0000          ZBLOCK  7400-.                  /THE FIRST 0020 WORDS OF BLOCK 0000 LOAD HERE.
  585   
  586           7400          STARTIT=.                       /THE REST OF THE WORDS IN BLOCK 0000 LOAD
  587                 /                                       HERE.  CONTROL IS TRANSFERRED HERE AFTERWARDS.
  588                 /                                       ALL /COMPATIBLE OPERATING SYSTEMS NEED TO BE
  589                 /                                       AWARE OF THIS OFFSET LOADING AND PROVIDE A
  590                                                         /SYSTEM-SPECIFIC PROCESS TO CONTINUE THE OVERALL
  591                                                         /OPERATING SYSTEM LOADING PROCESS.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 14

  593                 /       NOTES:
  594   
  595                 /       1)  THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP ALSO LOADS THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0001 INTO
  596                 /           07600-07777; THIS IS ONLY MEANINGFUL TO OS/8 AND COS-300/310.
  597   
  598                 /       2)  THE MR8E-C ROM BOOTSTRAP FUNCTIONS IDENTICALLY TO THE STANDARD DEC TD8E
  599                 /           BOOTSTRAP; CLEARLY THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP IS THE TEMPLATE FOR THE
  600                 /           DESIGN OF THE ROM-BASED ROUTINES.
  601   
  602                 /       3)  THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP IS NOT WELL DEVELOPED.  IT CAN BE MADE
  603                 /           MORE ROBUST BY CHANGING THE "K1000" SYMBOLIC REFERENCE TO THE WORD AT
  604                 /           "GET+1" [WHICH WOULD MAKE IT SELF-REFERENTIAL].  THE ONLY REQUIREMENT OF
  605                 /           THE CONSTANT USED IS THE HIGH-ORDER FOUR BITS ARE 0, 0, 1, 0; AS WRITTEN,
  606                 /           EITHER LOCATION ACCOMPLISHES THIS; ONCE THIS CHANGE IS MADE, ADDITIONAL
  607                 /           CHANGES ARE POSSIBLE TO MAKE THIS PROGRAM MORE ROBUST [BY ITSELF, THIS
  608                 /           CHANGE IS MERELY INNOCUOUS].
  609   
  610                 /       4)  ASSUMING 3) ABOVE HAS BEEN PERFORMED, THE INSTRUCTION AT 07300 CAN BE
  611                 /           CHANGED TO "CLA CLL CML RTR" WHICH LOADS THE ACCUMULATOR WITH 2000 [AKA
  612                 /           "NL2000"].  THIS CHANGE HAS THE ADDED BENEFIT OF ENSURING THE PROPER
  613                 /           CONTENTS OF THE AC AS THE PROGRAM STARTS, WITHOUT RELIANCE ON POWER CLEAR
  614                 /           CONSIDERATIONS [WHICH COULD BE IMPROPERLY CARRIED OUT BY USERS UNFAMILIAR
  615                 /           WITH THE PROCESS].
  616   
  617                 /       5)  ASSUMING 3) AND 4) ABOVE HAVE BEEN PERFORMED, THE CONTENTS OF "GET" BECOME
  618                 /           UNIMPORTANT.  THIS ALLOWS THE FRONT PANEL OPERATIONS NEEDED TO TOGGLE IN
  619                 /           THIS CODE TO BE ONE OPERATION SHORTER [THE PREVIOUS VALUE CAN BE LEFT ON
  620                 /           THE FRONT PANEL SWITCHES THEN PRESS DEPOSIT TWICE].
  621   
  622                 /       IT IS CLEAR THIS BOOTSTRAP WAS NOT OPTIMIZED AS IS USUALLY THE CASE WITH OTHER
  623                 /       DEC BOOTSTRAP CODING; HOWEVER, IT IS KNOWN THAT AT THE TIME THE TD8E WAS FIRST
  624                 /       PRODUCED, THERE WAS WIDESPREAD PROGRAMMER APATHY OR EVEN OPEN DISDAIN FOR THE
  625                 /       DEVICE.  THE NON-ROM VERSION OF A DEVICE HANDLER FOR OS/8 TO SUPPORT THE TD8E
  626                 /       [THAT REQUIRES AT LEAST 12K OF MEMORY] IS DOCUMENTED IN SURVIVING OS/8 SOURCE
  627                 /       FILES AS "THE TD8E PROBLEM".  THIS ALSO IMPACTED NEGATIVELY ON SUBSEQUENT
  628                 /       DEVICE HANDLERS ALSO REQUIRING AT LEAST 12K OF MEMORY; THE HANDLERS FOR THESE
  629                 /       NEWER DEVICES WERE PRAGMATICALLY WRITTEN TO SUPERFICIALLY MIMIC QUIRKS OF THE
  630                 /       TD8E HANDLER.  THIS BECAME NECESSARY TO ALLOW CERTAIN PROGRAMS TO HANDLE "THE
  631                 /       TD8E PROBLEM" GENERICALLY EVEN IF THIS REQUIREMENT WAS DETRIMENTAL TO THE
  632                 /       HANDLERS FOR THESE OTHER DEVICES.
  633   
  634                 /       IT WAS SUGGESTED TO THE PDP-8 PROGRAMMING STAFF THAT OS/8 BE REWRITTEN TO
  635                 /       CONFORM TO THE EMERGING P?S/8 MEMORY MANAGEMENT STANDARD USED IN ALL P?S/8
  636                 /       RELEASES FROM THAT ERA TO THE PRESENT; THEY CONSIDERED IT A GOOD IDEA BUT TOO
  637                 /       MUCH WORK TO BOTHER WITH.  AS SUCH, THE RELEVANT RELEASES OF OS/8 BASIC AND
  638                 /       FORTRAN IV HAVE WEAKNESSES WITHIN THEM DIRECTLY TRACEABLE TO THIS "PROBLEM".


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 15

  640                 /       3.      P?S/8 TD8E BOOTSTRAP.
  641   
  642                 /       THIS BOOTSTRAP IS ONLY FOR P?S/8 SYSTEMS BASED ON THE TD8E DECTAPE CONTROLLER.
  643                 /       THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP WILL ALSO WORK; HOWEVER, IT CANNOT ACCESS
  644                 /       DRIVE UNIT 1 AS AN ALTERNATE BOOTUP DEVICE CHOICE.  [NOTE: THE CODE PRESENTED
  645                 /       HERE DOES NOT ACTUALLY BOOTUP DRIVE UNIT 1; IT IS HOPED THAT FUTURE RELEASES
  646                 /       OF P?S/8 FOR TD8E WILL BE COMPATIBLE WITH THIS CODE WITH SUITABLE CHANGES MADE
  647                 /       THAT WILL SUPPORT DRIVE UNIT 1.]  [NOTE: SUPPORT FOR DRIVE UNIT 1 BOOTUP IN
  648                 /       THE P?S/8 TD8E/MR8E-C CONFIGURATION IS CURRENTLY UNDER DEVELOPMENT; IT MAY
  649                 /       PROVE IMPOSSIBLE GIVEN THE NEED TO SOLVE THE FATAL FLAW IN THE PRESENT CODE AS
  650                 /       WAS RECOVERED FROM THE SPECIFIC DECTAPE IN QUESTION.  THIS BOOTSTRAP MAY
  651                 /       BECOME WORTHLESS AS THE FATAL FLAW IS REMOVED, OR PERHAPS MIGHT BE USEFUL
  652                 /       WHERE IT IS POSSIBLY NEEDED, NAMELY ON THE TD8E CONFIGURATION WITH 8K OR MORE
  653                 /       MEMORY WITHOUT THE MR8E-C ROM; FOR THE PRESENT IT IS RETAINED FOR REFERENCE
  654                 /       PURPOSES ONLY.]
  655   
  656                 /       THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP IS SELFISHLY DESIGNED TO ALLOW OS/8 BOOTUP
  657                 /       EASIER AT THE EXPENSE OF OTHER SYSTEMS COMPATIBLE WITH THIS CONVENTION; AS
  658                 /       SUCH, IT IS NEEDLESSLY INFLEXIBLE.  [NUANCES OF OTHER SYSTEMS SUCH AS MULTIPLE
  659                 /       DRIVE UNIT SUPPORT CANNOT BE IMPLEMENTED.]
  660   
  661                 /       THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP LOADS THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0001 INTO
  662                 /       07600-07777 WHERE OS/8 [AND COS-300/310] REQUIRE THIS; THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK
  663                 /       0000 ARE LOADED INTO 07360-07557 WHICH IS OF NO PARTICULAR ADVANTAGE TO ANY
  664                 /       SUPPORTED SYSTEM [AND TENDS TO CAUSE NEEDLESS BOOTUP COMPLEXITY].  AS SUCH,
  665                 /       FOR ALL SUPPORTED SYSTEMS [INCLUDING OS/8 AND COS-300/310], WHATEVER ASPECT OF
  666                 /       BLOCK 0000 REQUIRING PROPER PAGE ALIGNMENT [GENERALLY TO 7600-7777, AND IN THE
  667                 /       CASES OF OS/8 AND COS-300/310 INTO FIELD 1] MIGHT BE NEEDED, IT IS NOT
  668                 /       PROVIDED.  IT IS NECESSARY TO COPY THE CONTENTS OF BLOCK 0000 TO THE PROPER
  669                 /       MEMORY LOCATIONS VIA ADDITIONAL CODING WITHIN EACH SYSTEMS DEVICE HANDLER
  670                 /       STRUCTURE.
  671   
  672                 /       IN THE CASE OF THE P?S/8 TD8E/MR8E-C SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER, THIS REQUIRES
  673                 /       HANDLER CODING TO SUPPORT THE CIRCUMSTANCES OF THIS ODD RELOCATION; MEASURES
  674                 /       ARE THEN TAKEN TO UNDO SPECIFIC CORRUPTION CAUSED BY THE MISALIGNMENT.
  675                 /       AFTERWARDS, THE HANDLER CODE IS COPIED TO THE INTENDED MEMORY LOCATIONS.  DUE
  676                 /       TO THE LIMITATIONS OF THE DEC STANDARD TD8E BOOTSTRAP, ONLY DEVICE UNIT 0 CAN
  677                 /       BE ACCESSED AT BOOTUP TIME.
  678   
  679                 /       THE P?S/8-SPECIFIC BOOTSTRAP CORRECTS THESE PROBLEMS BY PROPERLY LOADING THE
  680                 /       ENTIRE BLOCK 0000 CONTENTS DIRECTLY INTO 07600-07777 AS INTENDED.  THIS WILL
  681                 /       ALLOW FUTURE RELEASES TO POTENTIALLY SUPPORT BOOTING TO DRIVE UNIT 1
  682                 /       [ASSUMING PROPER REVISIONS ARE MADE TO ALL AFFECTED COMPONENTS].  THE PRESENT
  683                 /       VERSION OF THIS BOOTSTRAP IS SEVERAL WORDS SHORTER THAN THE DEC BOOTSTRAP.
  684   
  685                 /       NOTE: THE BUILT-IN BOOTSTRAP WITHIN THE MR8E-C ROM IS CONSISTENT WITH THE
  686                 /       DEC STANDARD TD8E BOOTSTRAP IN ALL RELEVANT WAYS.  ONLY THE P?S/8 TD8E
  687                 /       BOOTSTRAP HAS THE POTENTIAL TO ACCESS DRIVE UNIT 1 AS DESCRIBED ABOVE.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 16

  689                         NOPUNCH                         /PREVENT BINARY OUTPUT; THIS SECTION IS FOR
  690                                                         /DOCUMENTATION PURPOSES ONLY.
  691   
  692          *7544          *7544                           /STARTING ADDRESS OF BOOT CODE.
  693   
  694                 /       NOTE: THE FIRST WORD BELOW NEED NOT BE LOADED INTO MEMORY IF THE BOOTSTRAP
  695                 /       PROGRAM IS STARTED AT "BUTSTRT" [07562].  IT IS INCLUDED TO CAUSE THE LOWEST
  696                 /       LOADING ADDRESS TO BE AN ALTERNATE STARTING ADDRESS; THIS WILL MINIMIZE THE
  697                 /       INFORMATION NEEDED FOR AN AVERAGE USER TO SUCCESSFULLY START P?S/8 FOR THE
  698                 /       TD8E.  [NOTE: IT IS HOPED THIS BOOTSTRAP WILL BE COMPATIBLE WITH THE P?S/8
  699                 /       TD8E CONFIGURATION FOR USE WITH 8K OR LARGER SYSTEMS THAT DO NOT INCLUDE THE
  700                 /       MR8E-C ROM.]
  701   
  702   007544* 5362  GTMARK, JMP     BUTSTRT                 /JUMP TO REAL START.
  703   007545* 1345  GT1000, TAD     GT1000/(1000)           /ADD ON UNIT 0, GO BIT TO PASSED DIRECTION.
  704   007546* 6774          SDLC                            /LOAD COMMAND REGISTER TO START THE TAPE MOVING.
  705   007547* 6771  GTSRCH, SDSS                            /NEW LINE IN?
  706   007550* 5347          JMP     .-1                     /NO, WAIT FOR IT.
  707   007551* 6776          SDRC                            /YES, READ THE COMMAND REGISTER.
  708   007552* 0360          AND     GT77/(77)               /JUST MARK TRACK BITS.
  709   007553* 1375  TADGTCM,TAD     GTCMPVALUE              /GET END MARK [OR 40 MARK] COMPARISON VALUE.
  710   007554* 7640          SZA CLA                         /SKIP IF IT MATCHES.
  711   007555* 5347          JMP     GTSRCH                  /GO BACK IF NO MATCH.
  712   007556* 2353          ISZ     TADGTCMP                /LOOK FOR 40 CODE SECOND TIME THROUGH.
  713   007557* 5744          JMP I   GTMARK                  /RETURN TO CALLER.
  714   
  715   007560* 0077  GT77,   77                              /CONSTANT 0077.
  716   007561* 7577  GTCT,   SBOOT-1                         /WORD COUNT AND STORE POINTER.
  717   
  718                 /       THE BOOTSTRAP STARTS HERE [OR JUMPED TO FROM THE LOWEST LOADING ADDRESS].
  719   
  720   007562* 7332  BUTSTRT,NL2000                          /SET REVERSE DIRECTION BIT.
  721   007563* 4344          JMS     GTMARK                  /REWIND TAPE 0 INTO THE END ZONE.
  722   007564* 4344          JMS     GTMARK                  /READ FORWARD TO 40 MARK.
  723   007565* 6773  GTLOOP, SDSQ                            /QUAD LINE FLAG UP?
  724   007566* 5365          JMP     .-1                     /NO, WAIT FOR IT.
  725   007567* 6777          SDRD                            /YES, GET A WORD.
  726   007570* 3761          DCA I   GTCT                    /STORE INTO BOOT AREA [MINUS ONE].
  727   007571* 2361          ISZ     GTCT                    /DONE ENOUGH?
  728   007572* 5365          JMP     GTLOOP                  /NO, GO DO ANOTHER ONE.
  729   007573* 6774          SDLC                            /YES, STOP THE TAPE.
  730   007574* 7410          SKP                             /SKIP TO THE SMA SZA CLA CONSTANT.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 17

  732   007575* 7756  GTCMPVA,-22                             /REVERSE END ZONE MARK CONSTANT.
  733   007576* 7740          SMA SZA CLA                     /40 CODE MARK CONSTANT; THIS WILL SKIP THE NEXT.
  734   
  735                 /       THIS IS THE END OF THE BOOTSTRAP CODE TO BE LOADED. THE NEXT LOCATION WILL BE
  736                 /       SKIPPED BECAUSE THE CONTENTS ARE COPIED FROM THE BOOTUP DECTAPE MEDIA AND ARE
  737                 /       NOT TRUSTWORTHY.  [THE CONTENTS OF PART OF THE REVERSE PCC MARK DATA IS NOW
  738                 /       LOADED INTO 07577; THIS VALUE IS OFTEN 7777.]  THE NEXT LOCATION TO BE
  739                 /       EXECUTED IS 07600 WHICH NOW CONTAINS THE CONTENTS OF THE FIRST DATA WORD [AND
  740                 /       IS FOLLLOWED BY THE REST OF THE DATA WORDS READ IN FROM BLOCK 0000.]
  741   
  742   007577* 0000  AT7577, .-.                             /THIS GETS STORED INTO.
  743   
  744                 /       THE CODE FALLS THROUGH INTO THE BOOTUP CODE READ IN FROM THE DECTAPE.  AS
  745                 /       APPROPRIATE, THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER MAY BE MODIFIED TO BOOT TO DRIVE UNIT 1
  746                 /       [ASSUMING THIS IS SUPPORTED].
  747   
  748           7600          SBOOT=  .                       /SYSTEM BOOTS HERE.
  749   
  750                         ENPUNCH                         /RESTORE NORMAL BINARY OUTPUT.
  751   
  752                 /       NOTE: THIS BOOTSTRAP MAY NOT BE FEASIBLE DEPENDING ON THE INTERNALS OF THE
  753                 /       P?S/8 TD8E HANDLER WHICH IS UNDERGOING DESIGN CHANGES; IT IS CONCEIVABLE THAT
  754                 /       ELEMENTS OF THIS BOOTSTRAP MAY BECOME RELEVANT TO THE NON-ROM CONFIGURATION.
  755                 /       HOWEVER, IT HAS BEEN TESTED WITH THE RECOVERED [BUT FLAWED] TD8E/MR8E-C
  756                 /       DECTAPE WHICH USES A METHOD OF BOOTUP THAT IS COMPATIBLE WITH THIS BOOTSTRAP
  757                 /       [AS WELL AS THE STANDARD DEC TD8E BOOTSTRAP, WHICH IS LONGER].


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 18

  759                 /       TD8E/MR8E-C DECTAPE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.
  760   
  761           0000          FIELD   0                       /WHERE THIS LOADS WHEN GENERATED/EXECUTED.
  762   
  763          *7400          *GENAD1                         /REQUIRED FOR SYSTEM GENERATION PURPOSES.
  764   
  765          *7600          RELOC   SBOOT                   /WHERE THE CODE EXECUTES
  766   
  767   007600* 4240  SBOOT,  JMS     SYSIO                   /CALL SYSTEM I/O ROUTINES TO BOOTUP.
  768   007601* 7600          SBOOT                           /READ INTO 07600 AND ONWARD.
  769   007602* 2000  SBTFUN, 20^100+.-.                      /FUNCTION WORD; LOW-ORDER UNIT BIT MAY BE SET.
  770   007603* 0000          SYSBLK                          /BLOCK 0000 AND ONWARD.
  771   
  772                 /       ALTHOUGH SEEMINGLY A SUBROUTINE CALL, THERE IS NO ACTUAL RETURN TO THE CALLER.
  773                 /       ONCE INITIATED, DATA TRANSFERS OVERLAY MEMORY; KEY CONTROLLING ADDRESSES AND
  774                 /       OTHER PARAMETERS READ IN FROM BLOCK 0000 TAKE CONTROL OF THE OVERALL PROCESS
  775                 /       IN MEMORY.  THE ACTUAL TRANSFER IS 07600-03577 [USING ADDRESS WRAP-AROUND
  776                 /       KNOWN TO CONTINUE IN FIELD 0].  THE FUNCTION WORD IS SET TO READ 20 BLOCKS
  777                 /       INTO MEMORY [BLOCKS 0000-0017].  THIS INITIALIZES THE KEYBOARD MONITOR [AND
  778                 /       BUILT-IN LINE EDITOR], THE RESIDENT COPY OF THE TFS DIRECTORY AND THE KEYBOARD
  779                 /       MONITOR TRANSIENT COMMAND AREA.  [NOTE: FINALIZATION OF THESE SYSTEM
  780                 /       COMPONENTS IS PERFORMED WITHIN THE KEYBOARD MONITOR.]
  781   
  782                 /       ONCE COMPLETELY LOADED [AND MOVED BY THE KEYBOARD MONITOR FOR CERTAIN AREAS]
  783                 /       THE MEMORY LAYOUT IS AS FOLLOWS:
  784   
  785                  /      BLOCK[S]          MEMORY        FUNCTION
  786   
  787                 /         0000          07600-07777     THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER.
  788   
  789                 /       0001-0014       00000-02777     THE RESIDENT KEYBOARD MONITOR AND LINE EDITOR.
  790   
  791                 /          N/A          03000-06777     INTERNAL FILE BUFFER FOR THE LINE EDITOR.
  792   
  793                 /       0015-0016       07000-07377     CACHED COPY OF THE CURRENT UNIT TFS DIRECTORY.
  794   
  795                 /         0017          07400-07577     THE TRANSIENT AREA OF THE KEYBOARD MONITOR.
  796   
  797                 /       NOTE: THE TRANSIENT AREA SERVES SEVERAL PURPOSES.  THE CONTENTS AND USAGE
  798                 /       DEPENDS ON VARIOUS COMMANDS.
  799   
  800   007604* 0000  SWAL,   .-.                             /COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES '/A'-'/L'.
  801   007605* 0000  SWMX,   .-.                             /COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES '/M'-'/X'.
  802   007606* 0000  SWY9,   .-.                             /COMMAND-LINE OPTION SWITCHES '/Y'-'/9'.
  803   007607* 2316  SOUTFLS,2316/.-.                        /OUTPUT FILE COUNT ETC. WORD.
  804   007610* 2316  SDATE,  2316/.-.                        /SYSTEM DATE WORD.
  805   007611* 4000  SCRSIZE,4000/.-.                        /SYSTEM CORE SIZE.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 19

  807                 /       NOTES ON OUTPUT FILE COUNT, SYSTEM DATE AND SYSTEM CORE SIZE WORDS:
  808   
  809                 /       THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT WORD WILL BE REDEFINED IN P?S/8 VERSION 9A.  AS OF
  810                 /       VERSION 8Z, BITS[7-11] CONTAIN THE COUNT OF OUTPUT FILES IN THE PASSED FILE
  811                 /       LIST; HOWEVER, BITS[0-6] MUST BE 0000000.  BITS[1-6] WILL BECOME THE
  812                 /       HIGH-ORDER SIX BITS OF A REDESIGNED DATE WORD THAT COVERS 512 YEARS DIRECTLY.
  813                 /       BIT[0] WILL DETERMINE THE STATUS OF THE FILE AND COMMUNICATIONS AREA OF THE
  814                 /       OPTIONAL P?S/8 SHELL [CURRENTLY UNDER DEVELOPMENT].  AS SUCH, ALL CONFORMING
  815                 /       PROGRAMS MUST MASK OFF BITS[0-6] TO OBTAIN THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT.
  816   
  817                 /       THE FORMAT OF THE SYSTEM DATE WORD WILL BE MODIFIED TO FORM AN 18-BIT INTEGER
  818                 /       WHEN COMBINED WITH BITS[1-6] OF THE OUTPUT FILE COUNT WORD.  THIS WILL REQUIRE
  819                 /       ALL PROGRAMS THAT ACCESS THE SYSTEM DATE TO BE REWRITTEN.  THIS IS ALSO
  820                 /       SCHEDULED FOR IMPLEMENTATION IN P?S/8 VERSION 9A.
  821   
  822                 /       THE CORE SIZE WORD CONTAINS SEVERAL SETS OF MEMORY AND OTHER STATUS BITS:
  823   
  824                 /       BITS[0-2] CONTAIN THE PHYSICAL SIZE OF MEMORY OF THE SYSTEM.
  825   
  826                 /       BITS[3-5] CONTAIN THE MAXIMUM SIZE THE LOGICAL CORE SIZE CAN BE SET TO.  THIS
  827                 /       COULD DIFFER FROM THE PHYSICAL SIZE FOR SEVERAL REASONS SUCH AS THE PRESENCE
  828                 /       OF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IN THE PHYSICAL MAXIMUM FIELD, OR THE SYSTEM
  829                 /       DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES AN EXTENSION SUCH AS IN THE CASE OF THE TD8E SYSTEM
  830                 /       THAT REQUIRES 8K OF MEMORY OR MORE [BUT DOES NOT USE THE MR8E-C ROM].
  831   
  832                 /       BITS[6-8] CONTAIN THE CURRENT LOGICAL CORE SIZE.  THIS VALUE CAN BE SET TO
  833                 /       ANY VALUE FROM 0 UP THROUGH THAT FOUND IN THE MAXIMUM LOGICAL SIZE STORED IN
  834                 /       BITS[3-5].  THIS ALLOWS PROGRAMS TO BE TESTED IN RESTRICTED CONFIGURATIONS TO
  835                 /       MIMIC THE LIMITATIONS OF SMALLER MACHINES OR TO PROTECT THE CONTENTS OF MEMORY
  836                 /       FOR USER-DEFINED PURPOSES.
  837   
  838                 /       BIT[9] IS SET IF THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES A DEVICE EXTENSION.  THE
  839                 /       DEVICE EXTENSION OCCUPIES LOCATIONS 6000-7777 OF THE HIGHEST PHYSICAL FIELD OF
  840                 /       MEMORY.  [NOTE: CERTAIN SYSTEM PROGRAMS SUCH AS P?S/8 PAL CAN ALLOCATE
  841                 /       LOCATIONS 0000-5777 OF THE HIGHEST PHYSICAL FIELD IN CASE THE LOGICAL CONSOLE
  842                 /       IS DISABLED AND THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER REQUIRES THE EXTENSION.]
  843   
  844                 /       BIT[10] IS SET IF THE LOGICAL CONSOLE OVERLAY IS ACTIVE.  ENTRY POINTS ARE
  845                 /       IMPLIED WITH RESPECT TO SPECIFIC 12-BIT ADDRESSES; THE FIELD IS DEFINED AS ONE
  846                 /       FIELD MORE THAN THE FIELD VALUE IN BITS[3-5].  WHILE THIS IS GENERALLY
  847                 /       IDENTICAL TO THE FIELD REPRESENTED BY THE PHYSICAL CORE SIZE, THIS METHOD
  848                 /       ALLOWS MULTIPLE MEMORY FIELDS TO BE RESERVED FOR UNUSUAL CONFIGURATIONS.
  849   
  850                 /       BIT[11] IS THE LOGICAL ABORT SWITCH THAT ANY PROGRAM CAN SET TO SIGNAL PROGRAM
  851                 /       EXIT BY ABORT [GENERALLY CONTROL-C DETECTED ON THE SYSTEM CONSOLE DEVICE].
  852                 /       WHILE COMPATIBLE PDP-8 CONSOLE HARDWARE CAN PROVIDE THIS INFORMATION VIA THE
  853                 /       KEYBOARD FLAG BEING RAISED [AND THE KEYBOARD BUFFER CONTAINING THE CONTROL-C
  854                 /       CHARACTER], DECMATES ARE NOT CAPABLE OF THIS DUE TO THE INCOMPATIBLE KEYBOARD
  855                 /       HARDWARE ON ALL MODELS.  BY SETTING BIT[11] AS NECESSARY, FULLY CONFORMING
  856                 /       PROGRAMS CAN BE WRITTEN TO COMPLETELY FUNCTION ON ALL PDP-8 AND DECMATE MODELS
  857                 /       SUPPORTED.  [NOTE: P?S/8 ONLY SUPPORTS "FAMILY OF 8" MODELS WHICH EXPLICITLY
  858                 /       EXCLUDE THE PDP-5 AND PDP-8/S; THESE MACHINES ARE NOT COMPATIBLE WITH THE
  859                 /       ORIGINAL PDP-8 MODEL RELEASED IN 1965 WHICH IS CONSIDERED THE MINIMUM SYSTEM
  860                 /       THAT CAN BE SUPPORTED IN P?S/8 AND ALSO OS/8 WITH SUFFICIENT MEMORY.]


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 20

  862                 /       COMES HERE WITH INTERRUPTS OFF TO CONTINUE PROCESSING THE LATEST SYSTEM DEVICE
  863                 /       HANDLER CALL.
  864   
  865   007612* 6214  SMORE,  RDF                             /GET THE CALLER'S FIELD.
  866   007613* 1346          TAD     SCIDF/(CIF CDF)         /TURN INTO CIF CDF RETURN FIELD INSTRUCTION.
  867   007614* 3325          DCA     SFLDXIT                 /STORE INLINE FOR EXIT LATER.
  868   007615* 1640          TAD I   SYSIO                   /GET THE CALLER'S BUFFER ADDRESS.
  869   007616* 3351          DCA     BUFADRESS               /STASH IT FOR THE ROM ROUTINES.
  870   007617* 2240          ISZ     SYSIO                   /BUMP TO FUNCTION WORD.
  871   
  872                 /       NOTE: THE FOLLOWING INSTRUCTIONS ARE EXECUTED IN LOCATIONS 07400 ONWARD DURING
  873                 /       THE STANDARD DEC TD8E [OR ROM-BASED] BOOTSTRAP; THE EFFECTS OF THIS WILL BE
  874                 /       INDICATED IN THE COMMENTS ON THE MISALIGNED CODE AFTER THE NORMAL USAGE BELOW.
  875   
  876   007620* 6774          SDLC                            /STOP THE TAPE NOW.  [SEEMINGLY EXTRANEOUS.]
  877   007621* 7344          NL7776                          /MASK THE UNIT BIT OFF.
  878   007622* 0640          AND I   SYSIO                   /GET ALL OTHER FUNCTION WORD BITS.
  879   007623* 6775          SDLD                            /LOAD DATA REGISTER TO CONFORM WITH THE ROM.
  880   007624* 0327          AND     S70/(70)                /GET BACK FIELD BITS FOR CALLER'S BUFFER.
  881   007625* 1346          TAD     SCIDF/(CIF CDF)         /FORM "CIF CDF" INSTRUCTION TO CALLER'S BUFFER
  882                                                         /FIELD.  NOTE: THE "CIF" IS EXTRANEOUS BECAUSE
  883                                                         /THE INSTRUCTION FIELD WILL BE CHANGED TO 7.
  884   007626* 3250          DCA     GETFLD                  /STORE INTO "GETWRD" ROUTINE.
  885   007627* 1250          TAD     GETFLD                  /GET IT BACK.
  886   007630* 3255          DCA     PUTFLD                  /ALSO STORE INTO "PUTWRD" ROUTINE.
  887                 /       TAD I   SYSTEM                  /GET THE FUNCTION WORD AGAIN.
  888   007631* 5336          JMP     SMORE2                  /CONTINUE THERE.
  889   
  890                 /       THE FOLLOWING IS WHAT OCCURS WHEN THE ABOVE WORDS ARE LOCATED AT 07400 ONWARD
  891                 /       BECAUSE OF THE STANDARD DEC TD8E [OR ROM-BASED] BOOTSTRAP.
  892   
  893                 /       *7400                           /WHERE THESE WORDS EXECUTE.
  894   
  895                 /       DECTAPE DRIVE UNIT 0 IS STILL MOVING FROM THE LAST BOOTUP DATA TRANSFER.
  896   
  897                 /       SDLC                            /THE AC IS CLEAR; STOP THE DRIVE.
  898                 /       NL7776                          /AC SET TO 7776.
  899                 /       AND I   SYSIO&177+7420/(5654)   /MASK AGAINST THE RANDOM CONTENTS OF 05654.
  900                 /       SDLD                            /PUT JUNK VALUE INTO THE DATA REGISTER.
  901                 /       AND     S70&177+7420/(5625)     /MASK OFF SOME BITS.
  902                 /       TAD     S6203&177+7420/(2353)   /ADD WORTHLESS CONSTANT.
  903                 /       DCA     GETFLD&177+7420         /DESTROY "SROMGO" POINTER.
  904                 /       TAD     GETFLD&177+7420         /GET JUNK VALUE BACK.
  905                 /       DCA     PUTFLD&177+7420         /DESTROY "WRQUAD" ROUTINE RETURN INSTRUCTION.
  906   
  907                 /       THE DECTAPE DRIVE HAS CORRECTLY BEEN STOPPED; HOWEVER, TWO LOCATIONS OF THE
  908                 /       HANDLER HAVE BEEN DESTROYED.  THIS DAMAGE MUST BE REPAIRED BEFORE THE HANDLER
  909                 /       IS SAFE TO MOVE TO THE PROPER LOCATIONS.
  910   
  911                 /       JMP     SMORE2&177+7420         /CONTINUE IN DAMAGE RECOVERY ROUTINE.
  912   
  913                         ZBLOCK  7632-.                  /EMPTY SPACE [IF ANY].


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 21

  915                 /       THE SYSTEM LOADER STARTS HERE. VARIOUS ARGUMENTS ARE STORED AS NECESSARY TO
  916                 /       IMPLEMENT A VARIETY OF SPECIFIC TASKS [SUCH AS STARTING A SYSTEM PROGRAM OR
  917                 /       IMPLEMENTING SYSTEM PROGRAM OVERLAYS].
  918   
  919                 /       THE DEFAULT CONTENTS WILL SAVE ALL OF FIELD 0 IN BLOCKS 0020-0057 [WHICH IS
  920                 /       ALSO THE BLOCKS OF THE TWO FILES "%" [0020-0037] AND "$" [0040-0057]
  921                 /       RESPECTIVELY.  THIS DEFINES HOW CORE-IMAGES ARE HANDLED WITHIN P?S/8 WHEN
  922                 /       USING SUCH PROGRAMS AS "GET", "START", "ODT" AND "BSAVE".  THE CORE IMAGE MAY
  923                 /       ALSO BE MOVED TO TWO DESIGNATED TINY FILE SYSTEM [TFS] FILES TO DEFER SUCH
  924                 /       WORK TO A LATER TIME WHEN THE TWO FILES ARE RESTORED.  WHEN THE "GET" COMMAND
  925                 /       [OR EQUIVALENT] IS USED, THE PROGRAM STARTING ADDRESS IS 07632 TO IMPLEMENT
  926                 /       THIS DEFAULT ACTION.
  927   
  928   007632* 4240  SLOAD,  JMS     SYSIO                   /SYSTEM LOADER ENTRY POINT; DEFAULT VALUES
  929                                                         /SAVE ALL OF FIELD 0 THEN RESTART.
  930   007633* 0000  SCORE,  0000                            /BUFFER STARTING ADDRESS; DEFAULT VALUE
  931                                                         /IS LOCATION 00000. 
  932   007634* 4000  SFUN,   00^100+WRITE+.-.                /FUNCTION WORD; DEFAULT IS WRITE 40 BLOCKS FROM
  933                                                         /THE FIELD 0 BUFFER [LOCATIONS 00000-07777].
  934                                                         /AS REQUIRED, THE LOGICAL UNIT BITS WILL BE
  935                                                         /FILLED IN TO INDICATE THE BOOTUP UNIT.
  936   007635* 0020  SBLOCK, BINADR                          /STARTING BLOCK NUMBER; DEFAULT IS 0020.
  937   007636* 5637          JMP I   .+1/(SYSTART)           /START AT THE INDICATED STARTING ADDRESS.
  938   007637* 7600  SYSTART,SBOOT                           /STARTING ADDRESS; DEFAULTS TO THE SYSTEM
  939                                                         /RESTART ADDRESS.
  940   
  941                 /       THE DEVICE HANDLER I/O ROUTINES ENTER HERE.  THE CALLER MUST SET THE DATA
  942                 /       FIELD TO THE CALLING FIELD; THE CONTENTS OF THE AC AND LINK ARE IGNORED WHEN
  943                 /       ENTERED.  UPON RETURN THE AC WILL BE CLEAR; THE LINK CONTENTS ARE GENERALLY
  944                 /       NOT MEANINGFUL; HOWEVER, MOST P?S/8 SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLERS ALSO CLEAR THE LINK
  945                 /       [IF POSSIBLE].
  946   
  947                 /       SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER ENTRY POINT.
  948   
  949                 /       THIS ABSOLUTELY *MUST* BE AT LOCATION 07640.
  950   
  951                         IFNZRO  SZA CLA-. <ERROR .>     /ENSURE ENTRY POINT MATCHES "SZA CLA" VALUE.
  953   
  954   007640* 2530  SYSIO,  2530/MONSTRT                    /SYSTEM HANDLER ENTRY POINT.  INITIALIZED FOR
  955                                                         /THE BOOTSTRAP TO STARTUP THE KEYBOARD MONITOR.
  956   007641* 7301          CLA CLL IAC                     /CLEAR THE LINK AND SET AC TO 0001.
  957   007642* 6000  S6000,  SKON                            /SKIP THE NEXT IF INTERRUPTS ARE ON AND
  958                                                         /ALSO TURN THE INTERRUPT SYSTEM OFF.
  959   007643* 7001          IAC                             /AC=1 IF INTERRUPTS WERE ON, AC=2 IF
  960                                                         /INTERRUPTS WERE OFF.
  961   007644* 1242          TAD     S6000/(IOF-2)           /NOW HAVE "IOF" INSTRUCTION IF INTERRUPTS WERE
  962                                                         /OFF OR "ION" INSTRUCTION IF INTERRUPTS WERE ON
  963                                                         /BEFORE THE SYSTEM DEVICE HANDLER WAS CALLED.
  964   007645* 3324          DCA     SINTXIT                 /STORE IN LINE FOR EXIT LATER.
  965   007646* 5212          JMP     SMORE                   /CONTINUE THERE.


/     P?S/8 SYSTEM HANDLER TD8E/MR8E-C        P?S PAL V08S    SAT  05-MAR-16  PAGE 22

  967                 /       SUPPORT ROUTINES FOR THE ROM-BASED CODE; THIS CODE CANNOT BE MOVED.
  968   
  969   007647* 0000  GETWRD, .-.                             /GET A WORD FROM THE CALLER'S BUFFER ROUTINE.
  970   007650* 6201  GETFLD, .-.^10+CDF                      /WILL BE "CIF CDF XX" WHERE XX IS THE
  971                                                         /DATA FIELD OF THE CALLER'S BUFFER.
  972   007651* 1753          TAD I   BUFPTR                  /GET A WORD FROM THE BUFFER.
  973   007652* 6272          CIF     ROMFLD                  /GOING TO ROM FIELD.
  974   007653* 5647          JMP I   GETWRD                  /RETURN TO CALLER.
  975   
  976   007654* 7705  PUTWRD, READLP+6                        /PUT A WORD INTO THE CALLER'S BUFFER ROUTINE.
  977                                                         /THIS WORD IS INITIALIZED FOR DIRECT OVERLAY
  978                                                         /DURING THE BOOTUP OPERATION [PRESENTLY].
  979   007655* 6201  PUTFLD, .-.^10+CDF                      /WILL BE "CIF CDF XX" WHERE XX IS THE
  980                                                         /DATA FIELD OF THE CALLER'S BUFFER.
  981   007656* 3753          DCA I   BUFPTR                  /PUT A WORD INTO THE BUFFER.
  982   007657* 6272          CIF     ROMFLD                  /GOING TO ROM FIELD.
  983   007660* 5654          JMP I   PUTWRD                  /RETURN TO CALLER.
